PowerBench Lab is a portfolio-oriented redevelopment of an instrument-data
processing workflow. It demonstrates software engineering around converter
characterization, not a released commercial test system or device certification.

All distributed examples and demo measurements are purpose-built synthetic data.
No employer reports, raw instrument PDFs, personal CVs, confidential product
identifiers, or original spreadsheets are included. The demo loss equation is
illustrative only and is not fitted to any real device.

No employer, instrument vendor, or institution endorses this project.
Third-party packages retain their own licenses. See LICENSE for this project's
MIT license. Responsibility for permission to process or publish laboratory
inputs remains with the person supplying them.
